      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify a protocol, and I don't know of any that uses sertraline at 1000 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 200 mg, and doses in the range of 1000 mg have caused serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmias. A once-daily oral order at that dose could be given in full before anyone catches it, so I'm not comfortable entering it myself.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter it directly** in the EHR, using the high-dose protocol order set or the pharmacy override pathway. That way the pharmacist's documented review and the monitoring plan are attached to the order.\n- **Let me enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 200 mg once daily. You could then adjust it through the protocol.\n- **Add the protocol name or reference to the order note** if you want me to help with a different dose. I can put it in the note field.\n\nI can enter any dose up to 200 mg right away if you'd like."
      }
